      "answer": "Let $X\\sim\\operatorname{Binomial}(205,0.65)$. Here $np=133.25$ and $n(1-p)=71.75$, so the normal approximation is appropriate. The approximating normal distribution has mean $133.25$ and standard deviation $\\sqrt{205(0.65)(0.35)}\\approx6.829$. With continuity correction, $P(X\\le117)\\approx P(Y\\le117.5)=P(Z\\le-2.31)\\approx0.0105$. This is below 0.05, so the observation is unusually small under the claim and provides evidence against the claim that at least 65% disapprove.",
